1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Threatened by a ruthless demon, humanity was on the brink of destruction.

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:16,000
All seemed lost until a lone mage stepped forward and took up the fight.

3
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:28,000
After his triumph, he was hailed as the Wizard King, and his story became legend.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Yes, my magic allows me to manipulate blood as I please.

5
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:41,000
Ever since I cast that healing spell on you, I've maintained total control over your blood as well.

6
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:44,000
And now for your first order.

7
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:48,000
I want you to kill every one of these weaklings with your own hands.

8
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Do a perfect job and leave no one alive.

9
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:57,000
Under the control of the Queen of Witches, Asta tried to kill his friends.

10
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:59,000
Stop this! I'll make you a deal!

11
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:04,000
No. No matter where you run, your ties to me cannot be broken.

12
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:08,000
You are my daughter, after all. And family lasts forever.

13
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:10,000
What do you mean by that?

14
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:15,000
You're not my family. And you never were.

15
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:18,000
Cause the Black Bulls are my family!

16
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:19,000
Fools are my family!

17
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:24,000
Vanessa's fervent pleas on behalf of her companions awakened a new power.

18
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:32,000
At last, the Red Thread of Fate.

19
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:40,000
It dispelled Puppet's blood?

20
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:45,000
I can already tell. It'll always side with me and those I hold dear.

21
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Which means you and I don't have any ties.

22
00:01:50,000 --> 00:02:08,000
Please be with us.

23
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:13,000
.

24
00:02:15,440 --> 00:02:16,280
.

25
00:02:33,140 --> 00:02:35,340
.

26
00:02:35,340 --> 00:02:35,400
.

27
00:02:35,400 --> 00:02:35,920
.

28
00:02:35,920 --> 00:02:37,860
.

29
00:02:37,860 --> 00:02:47,620
履き潰した靴のレッシュアート 出発で一体どこだっけな

30
00:02:47,620 --> 00:02:53,780
いつかのページとひらぐった 言い訳ばかり探している

31
00:02:53,780 --> 00:03:01,720
毎日にさよなら告げるよ 走り出す列車に飛び乗った

32
00:03:01,720 --> 00:03:09,960
小さくては見えないけど 大丈夫さ そんな気がするんだ

33
00:03:31,720 --> 00:03:38,280
Your Majesty! Look! I made a doll out of my thread!

34
00:03:38,280 --> 00:03:41,480
Oh my! You've done a lovely job!

35
00:03:41,480 --> 00:03:45,480
I want to use my magic power to make other people happy!

36
00:03:45,480 --> 00:03:49,080
Well, how sweet! I'm sure you will, Vanessa!

37
00:03:54,360 --> 00:03:58,440
Somewhere along the way in my quest for absolute perfection,

38
00:03:58,440 --> 00:04:02,120
It seems that I lost sight of an extremely precious truth.

39
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:08,840
When one is imperfect, there is a certain kind of power that can be gathered from one's emotions.

40
00:04:10,040 --> 00:04:13,240
She could never have learned that spell during her time with me.

41
00:04:13,880 --> 00:04:19,400
But now that she is free to be her imperfect self, she's become perfect.

42
00:04:22,440 --> 00:04:27,400
Do as you see fit. It seems I must admit defeat.

43
00:04:28,440 --> 00:04:31,160
Blood recovery magic.

44
00:04:32,280 --> 00:04:34,760
Curse-breaking blood-filled cocoon.

45
00:04:58,440 --> 00:04:59,000
Blood recovery magic.

46
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:16,520
Hey, I'm all healed up.

47
00:05:18,760 --> 00:05:19,800
What just happened?

48
00:05:19,800 --> 00:05:26,120
It must have taken a lot of magic to do that.

49
00:05:27,480 --> 00:05:29,320
The Queen really is powerful, huh?

50
00:05:29,320 --> 00:05:42,600
Did we... win?

51
00:05:51,080 --> 00:05:53,080
You were so amazing, Vanessa!

52
00:05:53,080 --> 00:05:57,560
You did it! Your new spell saved all of us!

53
00:06:02,920 --> 00:06:04,040
I'm so relieved!

54
00:06:04,040 --> 00:06:07,800
Oh, Sel! So am I! You had me worried sick!

55
00:06:07,800 --> 00:06:10,600
I don't know what I'd do if I had lost you!

56
00:06:10,600 --> 00:06:12,040
Hey, everything's okay!

57
00:06:12,760 --> 00:06:14,760
Except that you're half-naked again.

58
00:06:14,760 --> 00:06:16,520
Oh, wow! Guess so!

59
00:06:18,360 --> 00:06:20,200
Long time no see, you two!

60
00:06:20,200 --> 00:06:21,240
Yeah, it's been a while.

61
00:06:26,440 --> 00:06:28,200
Nice work, you little tiger!

62
00:06:28,200 --> 00:06:31,720
All of this is thanks to you.

63
00:06:34,040 --> 00:06:34,920
No, it isn't.

64
00:06:36,680 --> 00:06:38,120
It was everyone here.

65
00:06:39,640 --> 00:06:42,040
My friends are the reason I could use that spell.

66
00:06:42,040 --> 00:06:44,840
Thank you all.

67
00:06:50,120 --> 00:06:51,000
Guess you're right.

68
00:06:52,920 --> 00:06:55,080
Hey, wait. I think... yeah.

69
00:06:55,080 --> 00:06:56,920
The pain's like 100% gone!

70
00:06:56,920 --> 00:07:00,360
My body feels even better than it did before this whole thing started!

71
00:07:00,360 --> 00:07:01,560
That's our Asta.

72
00:07:01,560 --> 00:07:04,200
Knock him down and he just gets right back up.

73
00:07:04,200 --> 00:07:06,920
And in case you haven't noticed, you need to put a shirt on!

74
00:07:07,560 --> 00:07:09,160
Crap, you're right!

75
00:07:09,160 --> 00:07:10,680
Who does that remind you of?

76
00:07:10,680 --> 00:07:12,280
I don't know.

77
00:07:12,280 --> 00:07:14,360
Come on, Noelle! This is cool!

78
00:07:14,360 --> 00:07:17,400
Now that I'm back to normal, my muscles are way bigger and stronger!

79
00:07:29,960 --> 00:07:30,840
This bird...

80
00:07:35,320 --> 00:07:38,200
I'm so happy all those bad guys are gone now!

81
00:07:38,200 --> 00:07:40,520
They're gonna be in big trouble if they come back!

82
00:07:45,560 --> 00:07:49,480
Apparently, the Eye of the Midnight Sun came here looking for a magic stone.

83
00:07:50,200 --> 00:07:51,400
Do you know where it might be?

84
00:07:51,400 --> 00:07:59,800
The magic stone you speak of is most likely this. However, it's of no use to me. You may take it.

85
00:08:01,400 --> 00:08:06,280
Are you serious? Thank you so much, Your Majesty! Wow!

86
00:08:06,280 --> 00:08:12,200
No way! I was not expecting it to be that easy! Yami's gonna be thrilled with us when we get back!

87
00:08:12,200 --> 00:08:18,200
Okay, so we know this is what the Eye of the Midnight Sun was after, but do you know why they would want it?

88
00:08:18,760 --> 00:08:22,520
Who are those guys and what are they trying to do? Got any info?

89
00:08:22,520 --> 00:08:29,000
That stone is a type of magic item that enhances the power of the individual who wears it.

90
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:32,440
But only a member of the Elf Tribe is able to use it effectively.

91
00:08:32,440 --> 00:08:34,280
Huh? Elf Tribe?

92
00:08:34,280 --> 00:08:43,720
They're quite gifted in magic. Many centuries ago, their kind resided in the place that is now known as the Forsaken Realm.

93
00:08:44,600 --> 00:08:51,560
Every member of the Elf Tribe was blessed with unbelievable magical prowess. Some even had capabilities that rivaled my own strength.

94
00:08:51,560 --> 00:08:57,560
She was alive then? So she's hundreds of years old? She really takes care of her skin!

95
00:08:57,560 --> 00:09:05,240
Sadly, they fell into war with the humans who outnumbered them, and the Elves were annihilated.

96
00:09:06,440 --> 00:09:12,280
The third eye that appeared on Fauna's head before she came to her senses is a kind of forbidden magic.

97
00:09:12,280 --> 00:09:18,200
However, Fauna was not the one who unleashed its power. She was merely a vessel controlled by another entity.

98
00:09:18,680 --> 00:09:21,720
Forbidden magic is beyond the reach of humans, you see.

99
00:09:22,280 --> 00:09:24,280
Okay, now you've lost me.

100
00:09:25,080 --> 00:09:31,320
The casting of a forbidden spell requires extraordinary mana, as well as some sort of sacrifice.

101
00:09:32,360 --> 00:09:39,000
For example, the ancient demon was summoned with the highest rank of forbidden magic by the leader of the Elves.

102
00:09:41,960 --> 00:09:43,240
Do you mean that demon?

103
00:09:43,240 --> 00:09:51,080
This Midnight Sun is a curious lot. I wonder if they might be descended from the Elf Tribe.

104
00:09:52,760 --> 00:09:57,800
Hold on. This is the clan of evil monsters in this storybook my grandmother read to me.

105
00:09:58,440 --> 00:10:00,440
Does this mean they were the Elves all along?

106
00:10:01,720 --> 00:10:05,400
All this important information is coming at us so fast, I can't keep up!

107
00:10:05,400 --> 00:10:07,960
If I don't take notes, I feel like I might forget everything!

108
00:10:07,960 --> 00:10:17,480
Listen well, Asta. The two weapons you carry are all that remain of the pair of magic swords once wielded by the leader of the Elf Tribe.

109
00:10:17,480 --> 00:10:20,360
I don't get it!

110
00:10:22,360 --> 00:10:26,360
Yikes! Looks like trying to follow that story made Asta's head explode!

111
00:10:26,360 --> 00:10:28,040
Get it together, birdbrain!

112
00:10:28,520 --> 00:10:31,000
His feeble mind can't handle much more of this!

113
00:10:31,960 --> 00:10:36,600
Should you continue to fight against the Midnight Sun, you may soon discover who they are.

114
00:10:37,720 --> 00:10:39,720
He doesn't short-circuit first!

115
00:10:39,720 --> 00:10:47,640
So, I guess you guys are going to head back to the Diamond Kingdom now.

116
00:10:47,640 --> 00:10:53,240
That's right. The Queen of Witches used her puppet's blood ability to create this special medicine for us.

117
00:10:53,880 --> 00:10:59,320
If I give it to the King disguised as a longevity potion, I should be able to thwart Morris' ambition.

118
00:11:00,280 --> 00:11:04,520
That way, I can reform the Diamond Kingdom into a peaceful nation.

119
00:11:04,520 --> 00:11:14,440
And I'll support Marzy Boy in pulling off this master plan of his. The only thing I've ever really cared about is making it to the top, and this seems like it's the fastest way to get there, right?

120
00:11:14,440 --> 00:11:17,160
Uh, are we sure about this guy?

121
00:11:17,160 --> 00:11:23,960
I'll try and become worthy of your approval. And then, I'll come back and see you, Teach.

122
00:11:23,960 --> 00:11:30,520
We'll look out for Fauna while you're gone. Be careful and try not to work too hard, okay, you guys?

123
00:11:30,520 --> 00:11:36,440
If you need us, we're here for you. I'll make sure he's not naked around her, or I'll try at least.

124
00:11:36,440 --> 00:11:45,160
Fauna, please. Will you wait for me? I'm going to set everything right. Someday, the Diamond Kingdom will be a place that you can come home to.

125
00:11:48,280 --> 00:11:55,480
I'll wait for you as long as I have to. And once Diamond is finally at peace, you and I will see the whole world together.

126
00:11:55,480 --> 00:12:13,400
Asta, I was glad when you said that I was your friend. If you're ever in trouble, I promise you, I'll be right there to help you out of it again, no matter what.

127
00:12:13,400 --> 00:12:18,680
No matter what. That's what friends are for, right?

128
00:12:18,680 --> 00:12:25,400
Yeah! And the same goes for me, too. Just say the word, and I'll bust into the Diamond Kingdom and save you!

129
00:12:25,400 --> 00:12:40,200
You are free, my child. But seeing as this is still your home, I would like you to come back and visit any time your heart desires.

130
00:12:40,200 --> 00:12:55,880
If you start off in second place, then the top will be there right in front of your nose.

131
00:12:55,880 --> 00:12:59,640
You'd better focus on helping Mars instead of just surpassing him.

132
00:12:59,640 --> 00:13:01,880
Yeah, yeah, yeah. I know. I know.

133
00:13:01,880 --> 00:13:03,880
This guy's a lost cause.

134
00:13:03,880 --> 00:13:05,880
Sorry I'm late!

135
00:13:05,880 --> 00:13:07,480
Oh, hey, Vanessa.

136
00:13:07,480 --> 00:13:13,320
Are you guys all done with your goodbyes? Not to rush, but I'd kind of like to get out of this creepy forest.

137
00:13:14,120 --> 00:13:18,600
Oh, rats. This place is crawling with girls and I didn't get a single date.

138
00:13:19,960 --> 00:13:22,760
Hey, what are you laughing at? Quit it!

139
00:13:22,760 --> 00:13:27,240
Thank you for healing, Asta. I hope you and I meet again someday.

140
00:13:27,240 --> 00:13:40,120
It's not that big of a deal.

141
00:13:40,120 --> 00:13:43,880
Oh, glad you made it back. Where'd your shirt go?

142
00:13:43,880 --> 00:13:45,880
You're so chill! What gives?

143
00:13:45,880 --> 00:13:50,280
Anyway, guess what? We found a magic stone! How cool is that?

144
00:13:50,280 --> 00:13:56,440
What? Listen, Asta. Now that you're patched up, your first mission is getting us more supplies.

145
00:13:56,440 --> 00:14:00,760
Sorry, yes sir! I'll grab everything we need and be back here in a flash!

146
00:14:00,760 --> 00:14:04,280
Wait a second. Don't tell me the rest of the team is still out there.

147
00:14:04,280 --> 00:14:06,600
What, you think someone's dead in a ditch or something?

148
00:14:07,400 --> 00:14:08,600
Maybe.

149
00:14:08,600 --> 00:14:13,160
Well, unless you want to die too, I suggest you hurry up and get shopping already.

150
00:14:13,160 --> 00:14:14,040
I'm on my way!

151
00:14:19,080 --> 00:14:19,560
Captain?

152
00:14:20,680 --> 00:14:22,360
Yeah, yeah. Welcome back.

153
00:14:25,960 --> 00:14:26,840
Thanks a lot.

154
00:14:35,880 --> 00:14:37,800
Hey, look what I bought!

155
00:14:37,800 --> 00:14:39,400
That quick? Creepy.

156
00:14:39,960 --> 00:14:41,880
Okay, boss. What's my next mission?

157
00:14:41,880 --> 00:14:48,360
Uh, rest up. You work too much. No more missions for a while.

158
00:14:49,720 --> 00:14:51,240
And put a damn shirt on.

159
00:14:51,240 --> 00:14:57,800
Oh, come on. If you take away my missions, what do I have to wear?

160
00:14:57,800 --> 00:14:58,680
Your muscles.

161
00:14:58,680 --> 00:15:01,720
There, there. Don't you think you're overreacting?

162
00:15:01,720 --> 00:15:05,400
Hey, when you're done being dramatic, I brought some clothes for you to wear.

163
00:15:05,400 --> 00:15:06,600
We're home!

164
00:15:06,600 --> 00:15:08,840
Look at that. They're still alive.

165
00:15:08,840 --> 00:15:11,640
That was definitely Magna's voice.

166
00:15:11,880 --> 00:15:18,760
Oh, right. He and Luck went into a dungeon looking for a way to fix my arms. I owe those guys a huge thank you.

167
00:15:18,760 --> 00:15:24,440
That must have been a heck of a trip!

168
00:15:24,440 --> 00:15:26,520
That must have been a heck of a trip!

169
00:15:28,520 --> 00:15:33,800
Our angel had lost his wings. And so we went adventuring. A risky thing.

170
00:15:33,800 --> 00:15:39,400
Wandering in the darkness, drowning in the loneliness, the breaking of my heart seemed endless.

171
00:15:39,400 --> 00:15:42,520
Then a vision of you came into view.

172
00:15:42,520 --> 00:15:47,160
Feeling you near, I let go of my fear and found the courage to push on through.

173
00:15:47,160 --> 00:15:49,240
This is way out of character!

174
00:15:49,240 --> 00:15:52,280
The mana is calling.

175
00:15:52,280 --> 00:15:53,640
Not you too!

176
00:15:54,520 --> 00:15:57,240
As the journey grew longer, my body grew stronger.

177
00:15:57,240 --> 00:16:00,280
And on through the dungeon we'd go, knocking down each and every foe.

178
00:16:00,280 --> 00:16:02,360
Yet there was one secret which we did not know.

179
00:16:02,360 --> 00:16:05,080
How could we hope to salvage your arms that had suffered such harm?

180
00:16:05,080 --> 00:16:08,520
By crushing regret, we were soon overcome, and that's when we knew we had to go home.

181
00:16:09,720 --> 00:16:11,080
The mana is calling me!

182
00:16:12,040 --> 00:16:13,960
But my arms are all better now, you guys!

183
00:16:17,400 --> 00:16:20,280
Well, that's great news, you jerk! Why didn't you tell us?

184
00:16:20,280 --> 00:16:21,480
Yeah, thanks anyway.

185
00:16:21,480 --> 00:16:24,200
Hey, good for you, Asta! Why don't we spar a bit?

186
00:16:24,200 --> 00:16:24,840
I'm good!

187
00:16:25,400 --> 00:16:26,040
We're back.

188
00:16:27,320 --> 00:16:33,400
It's Ghosh! Oh, I forgot, he and Gordon took a trip to the Royal Library to research a cure for my arms.

189
00:16:33,400 --> 00:16:34,680
I'd better thank them too.

190
00:16:37,240 --> 00:16:39,400
How they turned into a couple of nerds!

191
00:16:40,840 --> 00:16:44,200
My eyes have opened at last to the splendor of magic.

192
00:16:44,200 --> 00:16:46,360
Every spell is a grand work of art.

193
00:16:46,360 --> 00:16:48,440
Wouldn't you agree with me, Professor Gordon?

194
00:16:49,320 --> 00:16:51,640
What is happening to these people?!

195
00:16:54,520 --> 00:16:57,000
I still can't hear anything this guy says.

196
00:16:57,000 --> 00:17:00,280
But as the key to restoring Asta's arms has yet to be discovered,

197
00:17:00,280 --> 00:17:04,360
we simply must manufacture some sort of curse-canceling spell no matter how long it takes.

198
00:17:04,360 --> 00:17:06,440
Just you wait, Asta, we can make you whole again.

199
00:17:07,160 --> 00:17:09,000
Don't worry about it, I'm all good now!

200
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:16,040
What is wrong with you?! I told you that I would take care of it!

201
00:17:16,040 --> 00:17:19,560
Go get cursed again right now or else, you selfish little-

202
00:17:19,560 --> 00:17:22,360
Hey, are you okay there? Your nose is bleeding!

203
00:17:23,880 --> 00:17:25,720
That's because you made me angry!

204
00:17:25,720 --> 00:17:27,240
It's still going!

205
00:17:27,240 --> 00:17:28,920
It's fine! Just shut up!

206
00:17:28,920 --> 00:17:30,600
Ah, I know.

207
00:17:32,680 --> 00:17:37,320
It's when you focus your thoughts and energy on the happiness of someone who stared here.

208
00:17:37,320 --> 00:17:41,560
I realized this after spending so much time with you alone in a library.

209
00:17:43,640 --> 00:17:46,040
I think I might have just found the solution to our problem.

210
00:17:46,760 --> 00:17:48,280
No, that's not going to work.

211
00:17:48,280 --> 00:17:52,360
If that was right, you would be a sister, of course.

212
00:17:52,360 --> 00:17:55,560
You'd have secrets to be treated with Asta as well.

213
00:17:58,760 --> 00:18:01,800
Ridiculous. I need to look at Marie for a moment.

214
00:18:01,800 --> 00:18:05,160
Asta is as dear to you as your sister.

215
00:18:05,160 --> 00:18:09,320
Am I your sister, Asta's family team, which means Asta's friend,

216
00:18:09,320 --> 00:18:13,480
a term which refers to me in case that is clear, is also family.

217
00:18:13,480 --> 00:18:15,240
Yes, I understand.

218
00:18:18,280 --> 00:18:20,120
Wait, is that Sharma?

219
00:18:20,120 --> 00:18:22,360
Oh, baby mushrooms!

220
00:18:28,200 --> 00:18:29,320
Guess what, guys?

221
00:18:30,360 --> 00:18:32,840
I got infected with magic mushroom paris!

222
00:18:32,840 --> 00:18:34,280
Are you still eating?!

223
00:18:34,280 --> 00:18:35,720
Don't look at me!

224
00:18:35,720 --> 00:18:38,680
I can't transform now! This is so embarrassing!

225
00:18:38,680 --> 00:18:39,960
How is that embarrassing?

226
00:18:41,320 --> 00:18:44,120
Sharmy, you gotta stop eating those nasty things!

227
00:18:44,120 --> 00:18:45,560
I can't.

228
00:18:45,560 --> 00:18:49,160
Every time you eat one, three more pop up!

229
00:18:49,160 --> 00:18:50,920
One, one, there's plenty.

230
00:18:50,920 --> 00:18:52,120
Hard pass!

231
00:18:53,400 --> 00:18:57,720
Look! We picked up all kinds of delicious goodies for everyone in my shot!

232
00:18:57,720 --> 00:19:00,520
So you risked your life for some gross food?

233
00:19:00,520 --> 00:19:03,240
Yeah, but we didn't find a way to fix your arms.

234
00:19:03,240 --> 00:19:04,120
Sorry about that.

235
00:19:05,160 --> 00:19:06,520
What a surprise.

236
00:19:06,520 --> 00:19:08,760
Wait, what? Your bandages are gone!

237
00:19:08,760 --> 00:19:10,360
Does this mean you've already been healed?

238
00:19:10,360 --> 00:19:12,680
How did that happen? Oh, I'm so embarrassed!

239
00:19:12,680 --> 00:19:14,600
Is there anything that doesn't embarrass you?

240
00:19:15,640 --> 00:19:18,200
You know, now that we've got plenty of stuff to eat and drink,

241
00:19:18,200 --> 00:19:21,400
and I've taken that workaholic muscle head off duty for a while,

242
00:19:21,400 --> 00:19:24,120
I say we ought to use this opportunity to do it up big.

243
00:19:25,160 --> 00:19:26,680
I'm saying we party!

244
00:19:26,680 --> 00:19:28,520
All right!

245
00:19:32,760 --> 00:19:35,240
I'm so happy I can eat with my arms again!

246
00:19:36,040 --> 00:19:38,680
Oh, I just realized no one was around this morning,

247
00:19:38,680 --> 00:19:40,440
so those guys never got fed.

248
00:19:40,440 --> 00:19:41,720
You, get on it!

249
00:19:41,720 --> 00:19:42,280
On what?

250
00:19:45,160 --> 00:19:46,680
Hey there, what's up?

251
00:19:47,240 --> 00:19:48,200
You must be hungry!

252
00:19:52,520 --> 00:19:53,400
Not again!

253
00:19:53,400 --> 00:19:57,480
Oh yeah, there's laundry to do, too.

254
00:19:58,440 --> 00:20:00,680
Where am I supposed to hang all this stuff up?

255
00:20:01,640 --> 00:20:03,880
Hey, the cleaning hasn't been done yet, either.

256
00:20:10,040 --> 00:20:10,760
Hey, kid!

257
00:20:10,760 --> 00:20:11,400
Yes, sir!

258
00:20:13,560 --> 00:20:16,360
Who told you you could open the door, numbskull?

259
00:20:16,360 --> 00:20:18,200
Now go get me some toilet paper!

260
00:20:19,320 --> 00:20:19,960
Sorry!

261
00:20:23,400 --> 00:20:28,120
Okay, what's next?

262
00:20:28,120 --> 00:20:30,680
Captain Yami may have ordered him to rest up,

263
00:20:30,680 --> 00:20:33,640
but that hasn't slowed Asta down for a second.

264
00:20:33,640 --> 00:20:36,600
Yeah, what he lacks in brains, he makes up for in energy.

265
00:20:42,200 --> 00:20:42,680
It's true.

266
00:20:43,720 --> 00:20:44,920
This is the place for me.

267
00:20:44,920 --> 00:20:57,880
What did I gain by joining the outside world?

268
00:20:59,400 --> 00:21:00,920
A family to call my own.

269
00:21:00,920 --> 00:21:07,240
A family to call my own.

270
00:21:21,160 --> 00:21:25,880
Wow, I will not have the purpose to have the music outside.

271
00:21:25,880 --> 00:21:41,900
I'll make it true

272
00:21:41,900 --> 00:21:46,100
My song, my days

273
00:21:46,100 --> 00:21:50,880
This world, I'll make it true

274
00:21:50,880 --> 00:21:55,860
I'll make it true

275
00:21:55,860 --> 00:21:59,200
La la la,諦めない

276
00:21:59,200 --> 00:22:03,700
My song, my days

277
00:22:03,700 --> 00:22:08,220
音符を書き加えてく

278
00:22:08,220 --> 00:22:12,640
流れくなった道さのくらには

279
00:22:12,640 --> 00:22:20,360
輝ける明日を映すメロディー

280
00:22:25,860 --> 00:22:35,860
Clover Kicks!

281
00:22:39,080 --> 00:22:40,240
How come?

282
00:22:43,480 --> 00:22:44,760
What's bothering you?

283
00:22:45,120 --> 00:22:47,920
So if that salamander thing was surrounded by flames,

284
00:22:48,020 --> 00:22:49,920
how come Fauna didn't get burned to a crisp?

285
00:22:50,240 --> 00:22:51,440
Uh, because it's magic?

286
00:22:52,020 --> 00:22:54,760
Okay, and when we use Sea Dragon's lair to go underwater,

287
00:22:54,760 --> 00:22:56,380
how come our clothes never get wet?

288
00:22:56,880 --> 00:22:58,060
Again, it's magic.

289
00:22:58,560 --> 00:22:59,940
And if kelp grows underwater,

290
00:23:00,020 --> 00:23:02,100
then how come it doesn't turn the ocean into broth?

291
00:23:02,440 --> 00:23:06,060
Leave all of the culinary questions to the brilliant Professor Charmy.

292
00:23:06,140 --> 00:23:08,060
You see, the explanation is quite elementary.

293
00:23:08,140 --> 00:23:10,980
Kelp possesses a component within its cells known as glutamic acid.

294
00:23:11,060 --> 00:23:12,560
That's the stuff that produces a broth.

295
00:23:12,740 --> 00:23:14,900
Because of a characteristic we call selective permeability,

296
00:23:14,980 --> 00:23:17,440
kelp is able to take in only the materials necessary to survive

297
00:23:17,520 --> 00:23:19,040
and excrete everything that's extraneous.

298
00:23:19,120 --> 00:23:22,240
And since the broth-producing glutamic acid helps to keep the kelp alive,

299
00:23:22,240 --> 00:23:25,460
it remains inside the cells until the organism eventually dries up and dies.

300
00:23:25,580 --> 00:23:26,340
When that happens,

301
00:23:26,420 --> 00:23:28,620
it's cell-bursts open, releasing the glutamic acid,

302
00:23:28,700 --> 00:23:29,780
and creating the broth!

303
00:23:30,120 --> 00:23:32,340
Just say it's magic and leave it at that.

304
00:23:35,620 --> 00:23:37,500
I'm sure the Eye of the Midnight Sun

305
00:23:37,580 --> 00:23:39,860
is still trying to get their hands on the magic stones,

306
00:23:40,240 --> 00:23:42,280
but I wonder what they really hope to accomplish.

307
00:23:43,000 --> 00:23:44,660
Black Clover, page 66.

308
00:23:44,740 --> 00:23:47,140
The Secret of the Eye of the Midnight Sun.

309
00:23:47,140 --> 00:23:49,760
My magic is drinking like a fish.

